[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Comprehensive Guide to Internationalization (i18n) and Localization in Next.js"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Building applications for a global audience requires robust internationalization (i18n) and localization (l10n) strategies. Next.js provides powerful routing and rendering capabilities that make implementing multilingual support efficient and scalable."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Understanding i18n Routing in Next.js"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Next.js allows you to configure locales, default locales, and domain routing directly in your next.config.js file. This automatically handles URL structures like /en/about or /es/about."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"module.exports = {
  i18n: {
    locales: ['en', 'es', 'fr'],
    defaultLocale: 'en',
  },
};"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Managing Translation Dictionaries"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"To serve localized content, you should organize your translation strings into JSON files categorized by language and namespace. Create a directory structure in your project root."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"// locales/en/common.json
{
  "welcome": "Welcome to our application",
  "description": "Build fast web applications globally."
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Implementing Localized Pages with App Router"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"When using the Next.js App Router, it is standard practice to use dynamic segments for the locale (e.g., app/[lang]/page.tsx). This allows you to pass the resolved language down to your server and client components."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"// app/[lang]/page.ts
import { getDictionary } from '../../get-dictionaries';

export default async function Page({ params }) {
  const lang = (await params).lang;
  const dict = await getDictionary(lang);
  return (
    <main>
      <h1>{dict.welcome}</h1>
      <p>{dict.description}</p>
    </main>
  );
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Best Practices for Localization"},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always format dates, times, and currencies using the native Intl API to respect user locale conventions."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Avoid concatenating translated strings, as grammar structures vary significantly across different languages."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Leverage caching strategies for translation dictionaries to prevent unnecessary disk reads or network requests on every render."}]
